     kappa=  0.5 eps=1e-04:  INT = 0.0000000000+0.0329157221j   target = 0.0000000000+0.0329234512j
     kappa=  0.5 eps=1e-05:  INT = 0.0000000000+0.0329226782j   target = 0.0000000000+0.0329234512j
     kappa=  2.0 eps=1e-03:  INT = 0.0000000000+0.0328454929j   target = 0.0000000000+0.0329234512j
     kappa=  2.0 eps=1e-04:  INT = 0.0000000000+0.0329156457j   target = 0.0000000000+0.0329234512j
     kappa=  2.0 eps=1e-05:  INT = 0.0000000000+0.0329226705j   target = 0.0000000000+0.0329234512j
     kappa= 10.0 eps=1e-03:  INT = 0.0000000000+0.0327977822j   target = 0.0000000000+0.0329234512j
     kappa= 10.0 eps=1e-04:  INT = 0.0000000000+0.0329108747j   target = 0.0000000000+0.0329234512j
     kappa= 10.0 eps=1e-05:  INT = 0.0000000000+0.0329221934j   target = 0.0000000000+0.0329234512j
     => kappa-INDEPENDENT and -> (i/2pi) d'(s): LEMMA verified.
     CONSEQUENCE (the loophole-killer): in the exact quantum Langevin
     equation  Qdd + 2 gamma Qd + Omega_R^2 Q = -lambda phi_in(z(tau)),
     gamma = lambda^2/(8 pi) and Omega_R are (a,H)-INDEPENDENT at every
     coupling; the ONLY (a,H)-dependence of the exact interacting steady
     state enters through the NOISE correlator W_kappa = kappa-only.
     Non-perturbative resummation changes the VALUE of the response, not
     its kappa-only character.

==============================================================================
PART C: the no-go ODE (independent re-run) — now binding the EXACT G
==============================================================================
[C1] G + (a^2/kappa) G' = C a/(2pi kappa)  =>  G = (C*kappa/2 + pi*C1)/(pi*sqrt(-H**2 + kappa**2))
     Every solution knows H explicitly and has a pole at kappa = H (a=0).
     The EXACT resummed G(kappa; Omega_R, gamma) computed below is built
     solely from kappa-thermal correlators and (a,H)-independent (gamma,
     Omega_R): it cannot satisfy this ODE unless C = 0 (ordinary inertia).
     => the susceptibility structure m_resp ∝ a/kappa is excluded at
        EVERY coupling strength in the Gaussian class, not just at
        finite order: THE NON-PERTURBATIVE LOOPHOLE CLOSES HERE.

